<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propaganda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Propaganda Ministry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reich Ministry of Public <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> and Propaganda was created in March 1933 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-goebbels">Joseph Goebbels</a> to control German culture and public opinion. It directed the press, radio, film, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, music and art, issued daily instructions to newspapers and, through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-chamber-of-culture">Reich Chamber of Culture</a>, decided who could work in the arts. It promoted the Hitler cult, antisemitism and the war effort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reich-ministry-of-public-enlightenment-and-propaganda.jpg" alt="Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propaganda" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sandau · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1989-0821-502,_Joseph_Goebbels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
